My level 24 samurai, Musahsi, is trying to go on his first quest,
and gets the following message "a mysterious force prevents you
from descending".  I had some very good, then very bad luck, and
I suspect that my quest may be done without having ever gone on
it.  Let me know what you think.

spoilers...








































I obtained my quest artifact, the Tsurugi of Muramasa, from one
of my previous samurai ghosts, who got it by a water deamon at
a fountain.   When I got down the the level with the magic portal
to the quest level, I got a faint telepathic message, and went
down to see Lord Sato.  After killing all the hostile ronin, I
met Lord Sato, and he made a long speech, something about the
Tsurugi, then told me to be on my way after the amulet.  

After that, if I walked past him, he asked me how my search
for the amulet was going.  Looked around for a while and found
a secret door to a small room with a down staircase.  When I
tried to go down, I got the message "a mysterious force 
prevents you from descending".  Not too surprising, I thought,
as I was only level 9 at the time.  

Went back up to go get some more experience.  With such a nice
start, it didn't take long for Musashi to become very powerful
(+6 Tsurugi, strength 18/**, AC -21, with BDSM and cloak of
magic resistance).  Even found a helm of brilliance and enchanted 
it up to +5, however as it turned out even this much intelligence
wouldn't prevent him performing an act of INCREDIBLE stupidity...

While trying to put something into his fully-loaded blessed
bag of holding, I accidentally answered "yes" to the first 
question (do you wish to remove something from your bag) instead
of "no", then "yes" to the put something into question which follows.

At this point, you get the question asking what do you want to
remove, which presents a list of all symbols for item classes,
and the letters aAi.  However, there is no quit option at this
point.  So, I just hit return, as you get the chance to quit
when it presents the first item for loading into the bag.

At this point I got something like 

    "Do you wish to place your +6 Tsurugi into the bag [ynaq]?".  

Well, I accidentally hit 'a' instead of 'q'.  Uh-oh, I see my Tsurugi
go into the bag and get --more--.  Hit return, there goes 
Snickersnee --more--.  Not wanting to have to haul everything out of 
the bag, I try to stop by hitting control-c.  What does Nethack give 
you at this point:  

    "Do you wish to quit your game [yn]?".  

Of course I answered 'n'o.  Back to the list, so many --more--'s, 
I get tired of hitting return and hit escape to skip the messaages.

I became unburdened, which seemed normal for the circumstances,
but when I tried to apply my bag to take everything back out,
IT WASN'T THERE!!!!!!!!!!!!  Wait, what the hell could have
happened to it.  Search around a bit, nowhere to be seen,
then remember THAT unidentified wand I picked up a few levels
ago.  Shit!  You're probably thinking the same thing I am, it must 
have been CANCELLATION.

THANK GOD wands come before tools on the list, otherwise I 
would have lost my blessed tinning kit, key, unicorn horn,
spare BoH (with one potion of holy water), luckstone.

With no weapons at all, and only the clothes on my back
my level 24 Musashi trudges back up the dungeon, and down
to the magic portal.  Hopefully he now has enough experience
to go on the quest, maybe there'll be a Tsurugi at the end
of the quest.  

Well, I get back to the level with the magic portal, and no
telepathic message, not even a faint one.  Back down the portal,
no greeting when I reach the other end.  Over to Lord Sato, and
he asks me how my quest is going.  Shit.  Over the secret room,
try to go down the staircase, same "mysterious force prevents me
from descending".

QUESTIONSS

I have the sinking feeling that there is only one of a given
quest artifact per game, independent of how you come across it
(wish, bones, etc.).  

Furthermore, I get the feeling that having the quest artifact
prevents you from going on the quest at all, even if you never
went on it to obtain it.

To make matters worse, on the way back to Lord Sato, I stopped
off at an altar and prayed to make some holy water.  My god
choose that moment to give me the "Hand of Elbereth".  I was
carrying a puny elven broadsword I picked up along the way,
and wasn't even wielding it.  Had I been wielding a long sword, 
it would have become Excaliber, I believe.   Was this my only
chance at Excaliber? 

Do Samurais ever get good artifacts via #offering?  Even though
they are lawful, all I ever get are relatively wimpy artifacts
(Ogremasher, Werebane, Sting, Orchrist).   Valks seem to get
Mjollnir as their first artifact.  If I keep on offering, will
I ever get Vorpy or Mjollnir (I think they are both lawful)?

Is there anything I could have done to interrupt the process
of putting all my posessions into the bag, once I had began
it? 

And, how do you make the game remember what you named a previously
unidentified item, and give that name to subsequent items
that you find?  I had a wand of cancellation earlier, unidentified,
but named CANCELLATION.  Shouldn't subsequent wands (I think
in this case, jeweled wands) carry that name when I find them?

This was my best game and character of all-time.  Is there any
hope at this point, or should I just end my misery and quit
now?  Without a major named artifact I don't think I'll 
get through the Valley of the Dead, which I was half-way
though before all this happened.



